korgwm (6.1-4) unstable; urgency=medium

  * click-to-focus: managed windows now select BUTTON_PRESS, so a plain click
    focuses the window under the pointer.  Moving and resizing a floating
    window stays bound to Super+click.

 -- Dmitry Oboukhov <unera@debian.org>  Fri, 30 Oct 2026 15:00:00 +0000

korgwm (6.1-3) unstable; urgency=medium

  * Carry the fixes in the sources instead of quilt patches:
    - add the missing NAME POD section to X11::korgwm::Layout
    - add the focus_follows_mouse option (click-to-focus mode)
  * Install the packaged configuration to /etc/korgwm/korgwm.conf.

 -- Dmitry Oboukhov <unera@debian.org>  Fri, 30 Oct 2026 12:00:00 +0000

korgwm (6.1-2) unstable; urgency=medium

  * Add a focus_follows_mouse option so the window under the pointer is no
    longer focused unconditionally; set it to 0 for click-to-focus.

 -- Dmitry Oboukhov <unera@debian.org>  Fri, 30 Oct 2026 00:00:00 +0000

